# Thrustmaster T.Flight Hotas One, macOS, base switch in PC mode (USB 044f:b68d).
# In Xbox mode (044f:b68c) the device is not a HID joystick and X-Plane cannot see it.
# Axis order measured from the HID report descriptor on macOS:
#   0 X stick roll, 1 Y stick pitch, 2 Z throttle lever,
#   3 Rz twist grip, 7 Dial rocker paddle on the throttle, 4/5/6 unused by the hardware.
OS: Mac
Name: T.Flight Hotas One
ID: VID:0x044fPID:0xb68d
Display: T.Flight Hotas One

Assignments:
--------------------------------------------------------------
Axis 0: joy_use_roll
Axis 1: joy_use_ptch
Axis 2: joy_use_thro
Axis 3: joy_use_hdng
Axis 4: hidden
Axis 5: hidden
Axis 6: hidden
Hat Switch 0 Direction 0: sim/general/hat_switch_up
Hat Switch 0 Direction 1: sim/general/hat_switch_up_right
Hat Switch 0 Direction 2: sim/general/hat_switch_right
Hat Switch 0 Direction 3: sim/general/hat_switch_down_right
Hat Switch 0 Direction 4: sim/general/hat_switch_down
Hat Switch 0 Direction 5: sim/general/hat_switch_down_left
Hat Switch 0 Direction 6: sim/general/hat_switch_left
Hat Switch 0 Direction 7: sim/general/hat_switch_up_left

# Same body as the T.Flight Hotas 4, so its pictures fit.
